      "text": "This paddle wheel steamship vessel was originally made as a passenger ship and performed duties during the interim until being re-fitted as a liner, showboat, and advertising vessel.",
      "class": "CONFIRMED_FACT",
      "layer": "CONFIRMED FACT",
      "source": "Wikipedia — Cable layer",
      "role": "evidence",
      "verbatim": false,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_layer",
      "section": "List of cable ships",
      "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "C90",
      "text": "CS Anglia (1901–1902) custom built-ship used on the 1901–1902, first trans-Pacific telegraph cable by Telegraph Construction and Maintenance Company (Telcon.) CS Hooper, built in Newcastle, launched 29 March 1873 for Hooper's Telegraph Works, first cable ship designed to lay trans Atlantic cable, renamed CS Silvertown in 1881.",
